# Only the downloaded Rebrickable archives are throwaway. sets.json,
# barcodes.json, prices.json and contributed.json are what the app serves, and
# harvest-state.json is the resume list — the scheduled refresh depends on it
# to know what it has already fetched, so it has to be in the repo. Caching it
# in CI is not enough: GitHub evicts caches after 7 days unused and the refresh
# runs weekly, so a miss would restart the whole 19h crawl.
data/cache/

# Current market values stay on the harvesting machine. Barcodes, RRP and
# retirement dates are catalogue facts; aftermarket valuations are Brickset's
# own derived analytics, so they are not republished here. The app reads
# values.json when present and works fine without it.
data/values.json
